  "final_answer": "## Most Popular Open-Source Image Processing Tool on GitHub\n\nBased on my search of GitHub for \"image processing\" repositories sorted by **Most stars**, the most popular open-source image processing tool is:\n\n### 🏆 **lovell/sharp** — 32.7k ⭐ stars**\n\n- **Repository:** https://github.com/lovell/sharp\n- **Language:** JavaScript\n- **Stars:** ~32,720 (32.7k)\n- **Description:** \"High performance Node.js image processing, the fastest module to resize JPEG, PNG, WebP, AVIF and TIFF images. Uses the libvips library.\"\n- **Last Updated:** Yesterday\n- **Topics:** nodejs, javascript, svg, performance, image\n\n### Top 5 comparison for context:\n| Rank | Repository | Stars | Language |\n|------|-----------|-------|----------|\n| 1 | lovell/sharp | 32.7k | JavaScript |\n| 2 | WZMIAOMIAO/deep-learning-for-image-processing | 26.4k | Python |\n| 3 | containrrr/watchtower | 24.6k | Go (not really image processing — Docker updates) |\n| 4 | BradLarson/GPUImage | 20.3k | Objective-C |\n| 5 | T8RIN/ImageToolbox | 14.8k | Kotlin |\n\n**`lovell/sharp` is the most popular open-source image processing tool on GitHub** by star count among repositories matching the \"image processing\" query.",
